    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for samba",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for samba fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-6949: TSIG packet with crafted name compression can crash internal DNS server (bsc#1271672).\n- CVE-2026-15779: `pam_winbind` module with `mkhomedir` set allows `chown` of critical system paths without validation\n  (bsc#1271469).\n- CVE-2026-58216: 6-byte heap OOB read in packet parser of the `kpasswd` service (bsc#1271674).\n- CVE-2026-58218: DNS TKEY negotiation stores unauthenticated GSS contexts in a fixed FIFO before authentication\n  completes (bsc#1271675).\n- CVE-2026-58221: authenticated LDAP access to internal LDB special DNs permits domain takeover (bsc#1271676).\n- CVE-2026-58222: LDAP Compare filter injection and trusted-request confusion disclose protected attributes\n  (bsc#1271677).\n- CVE-2026-58224: heap OOB read due to unchecked packet length fields in CTDB (bsc#1271673).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SL-Micro-6.2-1386",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
